<title>EGYPT: Egypt cuts three Jan crude prices 10-15 cents.</title>
<headline>Egypt cuts three Jan crude prices 10-15 cents.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egypt raised the January price of its Gulf of Suez Blend by 25 U.S. cents and also cut prices for three other grades by between 10 and 15 cents, the state's Egyptian General Petroleum Corp (EGPC) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The prices of two other grades were unchanged from December against Dated Brent, the official said.  </p>
<p>Following are details of EGPC's January crude prices (December differentials in brackets):</p>
<p>    Gulf of Suez    -$2.10  (-$2.35)</p>
<p>    Belayim	   -$3.35  (-$3.20)</p>
<p>    Ras Gharib	-$4.20  (-$4.10)</p>
<p>    Ras Badran	-$3.65  (-$3.50)</p>
<p>    Ras el Behar    -$1.60  (-$1.60)</p>
<p>    Zeit Bay	  -$1.65  (-$1.65)</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +202 578 3290/91</p>
